        "The average negative log-likelihood is also the empirical cross-entropy of the observed data relative to the model.\n",
        "\n",
        "## Entropy\n",
        "\n",
        "Entropy measures uncertainty in a probability distribution.  For a distribution $p$ on $V$, the entropy is\n",
        "\n",
        "$$\n",
        "H(p)=-\\sum_{j=1}^d p_j\\log p_j.\n",
        "$$\n",
        "\n",
        "We use the convention $0\\log 0=0$, interpreted as a limit.\n",
        "\n",
        "If $p$ is concentrated on one token, entropy is small.  If $p$ is spread evenly across many tokens, entropy is large.\n",
        "\n",
        "### Example\n",
        "\n",
        "For a four-token vocabulary, compare\n",
        "\n",
        "$$\n",
        "p=(1,0,0,0)\n",
        "$$\n",
        "\n",
        "and\n",
        "\n",
        "$$\n",
        "q=\\left(\\frac14,\\frac14,\\frac14,\\frac14\\right).\n",
        "$$\n",
        "\n",
        "Then\n",
        "\n",
        "$$\n",
        "H(p)=0,\n",
        "$$\n",
        "\n",
        "while\n",
        "\n",
        "$$\n",
        "H(q)=-4\\left(\\frac14\\log\\frac14\\right)=\\log 4.\n",
        "$$\n",
        "\n",
        "The uniform distribution has the largest entropy among distributions on four outcomes.\n",
        "\n",
        "### Python example: entropy of token distributions"
      ],
      "id": "648dba8d"
    },
