        "## Log probabilities and numerical stability\n",
        "\n",
        "Products of many probabilities become extremely small.  For a sentence of length $T$, the probability\n",
        "\n",
        "$$\n",
        "\\prod_{t=1}^T p_\\theta(w_t\\mid w_{1:t-1})\n",
        "$$\n",
        "\n",
        "may underflow on a computer.  Therefore NLP systems usually work with log probabilities:\n",
        "\n",
        "$$\n",
        "\\log \\prod_{t=1}^T p_\\theta(w_t\\mid w_{1:t-1})\n",
        "=\n",
        "\\sum_{t=1}^T \\log p_\\theta(w_t\\mid w_{1:t-1}).\n",
        "$$\n",
        "\n",
        "Log probabilities turn products into sums, making computation more stable and easier to optimize.\n",
        "\n",
